<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lê Hiến Tông</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1461">1461</a>–<a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Le Hien Tong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lê Hiến Tông was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Later Lê dynasty from 1497 to 1504. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong">Lê Thánh Tông</a>, he preserved his father's Confucian institutions and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-examination">examination system</a>, and his reign is counted as the last of the dynasty's stable period before decades of misrule and revolt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-hien-tong.jpg" alt="Lê Hiến Tông" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 阮朝國史館（Quốc sử quán triều Nguyễn） · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E3%80%8A%E6%AC%BD%E5%AE%9A%E8%B6%8A%E5%8F%B2%E9%80%9A%E9%91%91%E7%B6%B1%E7%9B%AE%E3%80%8B%E5%8D%B7%E9%A6%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
